        "answer": {
          "short": "$y = 2x - 3$",
          "worked": "Each time $x$ increases by $1$, $y$ changes by $2$, so $m=2$. Extend the table forward to $x=0$, adding $2$ for each step: $y$-values $-13, -11, -9, -7, -5, -3$. Hence $c=-3$.\n\n$y = 2x - 3$\n\nCheck another column: at $x=-1$, the rule gives $y=-5$, matching the table.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
